                         you set the rules

  Already run your own reverse proxy, such as SWAG, Pangolin, Nginx Proxy Manager, Traefik or
  Caddy? Choosing this changes nothing here. Run self-host access export to print where each App
  lives, then give it to your proxy. You stay in charge of names, certificates and who gets in.
  Home network keeps working. This one is for advanced users.

  Who is this for?
  Advanced users who already run a reverse proxy, such as SWAG, Pangolin, Nginx Proxy Manager,
  Traefik or their own Caddy, or want to run one. You keep control of names, certificates and who
  gets in.

  Getting the settings
  Run self-host access export --format caddy, nginx, traefik or json. It prints each App's name,
  where it lives and a hostname to replace with your own. It changes nothing: copy what it prints
  into your proxy.

  Home network keeps working

